{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794054253,"nonce":"FshVhyoEQn9QwpLExhSsxpr7vps=","title":"Two approvals that meet an Environment's rules at once write two deployment records","message":"Split from 16c48e1 (its fourth point).\n\napprove_gate (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs, step 4) reads environment_approval_met from the event log and calls record_deployment when none is recorded yet. Two approvals that complete the rules concurrently both read none, so both append EnvironmentApprovalMet and both write a record to the legacy deployment history (GET …/environments/{name}/deployments). The same race exists on main before #101.\n\nFix options:\n- a uniqueness key on the history: add the gate step and the wait's start to scarab_project::Deployment, with a unique index (a migration), and treat a conflict as done;\n- or append EnvironmentApprovalMet conditionally (once per wait) and let only the approval whose append won write the record.\n\nEvidence: ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261107-0247-decisions/review/safety.md; run.md C-04 note (\"the known double record on a race stands\").","files":null}]}